From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] server: Don't send WM_MOUSEMOVE for relative moves that the cursor clip cancels out.

Absolute moves to the current position don't generate WM_MOUSEMOVE, but
relative ones pushing against the clip rectangle did: winewayland sends
relative moves while the pointer is locked, so Lords of Magic got hundreds of
mouse messages per second while holding its cursor at a screen edge, which
made its map scroll very slowly. Clamp relative moves to the clip rectangle
before comparing them with the current position, for messages only: raw input
still gets the motion.
---
diff -ruN a/server/queue.c b/server/queue.c
--- a/server/queue.c
+++ b/server/queue.c
@@ -2324,6 +2324,20 @@
 
     if (send_flags & SEND_HWMSG_NO_MSG) return 0;
 
+    /* a relative move against the clip rectangle doesn't move the cursor, so
+     * don't send WM_MOUSEMOVE for it, as for absolute moves (Lords of Magic
+     * scrolls its map slowly while it gets them with the cursor at an edge) */
+    if ((flags & MOUSEEVENTF_MOVE) && !(flags & MOUSEEVENTF_ABSOLUTE))
+    {
+        struct rectangle clip = desktop_shm->cursor.clip;
+        int clip_x = max( min( x, clip.right - 1 ), clip.left );
+        int clip_y = max( min( y, clip.bottom - 1 ), clip.top );
+
+        if (clip_x == desktop_shm->cursor.x && clip_y == desktop_shm->cursor.y &&
+            (!win || desktop->cursor_win == win))
+            flags &= ~MOUSEEVENTF_MOVE;
+    }
+
     for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE( messages ); i++)
     {
         if (!messages[i]) continue;
